# What:  Paths Prettier must NOT format. Mirrors .gitignore conceptually but
#        scoped to formatter behavior.
# Why:   - pnpm-lock.yaml: pnpm regenerates it in canonical single-quote form
#          on every install; prettier rewriting to double-quote causes a
#          drift loop on every pre-commit run.
#        - Build / cache / dependency dirs: never authored by us.
#        - eslint fixtures: intentional violations; reformatting could mask
#          the very pattern the linter is meant to detect.
# Where: Loaded by `prettier` CLI and `prettier --write` invocations from
#        lint-staged in .husky/pre-commit (Layer 2 of defense-in-depth).
# When:  Every pre-commit hook run, every manual `pnpm exec prettier ...`,
#        every editor-save when Prettier extension respects this file.

# Lockfiles (regenerated by package manager — never hand-format)
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Generated / cached output
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/

# ESLint red-team fixtures: intentional violations; do not auto-format
__tests__/__fixtures__/
